# Hearth COSMIC on Anatase (Fedora): what os-bases/anatase/build.sh and cosmic-test.yml install. One package a line;
# lines starting with "-" are left out (--exclude). docs/COSMIC.md says why each is or isn't here.
# COSMIC's workspace
cosmic-session
cosmic-comp
cosmic-panel
cosmic-settings
cosmic-settings-daemon
cosmic-launcher
cosmic-applets
cosmic-bg
cosmic-osd
cosmic-notifications
cosmic-workspaces
cosmic-app-library
cosmic-randr
cosmic-idle
cosmic-icon-theme
xdg-desktop-portal-cosmic
# COSMIC's own apps for the kinds it has (in COSMIC they take the place of Hearth Files, Terminal and Text)
cosmic-files
cosmic-term
cosmic-edit
# cosmic-session needs COSMIC's on-screen keyboard installed; Hearth's is the one used (not on the panel)
cosmic-osk
# Left out: COSMIC's login screen (Anatase's stays), first-run wizard, and apps of kinds Hearth already has
-cosmic-greeter
-greetd
-cosmic-initial-setup
-cosmic-store
-cosmic-player
-cosmic-wallpapers
-cosmic-monitor
